- action(n1, "Start the process"): Hallucinates a preliminary step; the description explicitly states "the process begins with picking flowers," meaning initiation should lead directly to the picking action without an intervening node.
- action(n5, "End Process"): Hallucinates a terminal step; the description indicates the process simply terminates after giving the bouquet to auntie ("Finally, the process comes to an end"), with no explicit intermediate action described.
- actor(a_default, "Default", [i1, n1, n2, n3, n4, n5, e1]): Misattributes responsibility; the source specifies "For Person F," requiring the actor declaration to reflect Person F rather than a generic "Default" participant.
- precedence(i1, n1), precedence(n1, n2), precedence(n4, n5), precedence(n5, e1): Distort source chronology by routing control flow through the hallucinated start/end actions instead of preserving the direct sequential progression outlined in the text.